# This file is a pointer, not configuration. Nothing in it is ever loaded.
#
# The console takes its environment from the repository-root `.env`: `apps/console/vite.config.ts`
# builds on `@seamnex/config/vite/app`, which sets `envDir` to the repository root and `envPrefix` to
# `VITE_`. An `.env` in this directory is therefore never read — copying this file to
# `apps/console/.env` changes nothing, and neither does `.env.local`.
#
# Where the values live:
#   ../../.env    `pnpm dev` writes it from ../../.env.example on first run; or copy it yourself.
#
# The console reads three variables, all documented at the root:
#
#   VITE_API_MODE      `mock` (default in development) runs the in-browser MSW platform;
#                      `live` talks to the real API through the `/api/v1` proxy.
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL  Vite dev-proxy target, and the API origin a production build talks to.
#   VITE_PORTAL_URL    Portal origin used by the console's "Open the portal" affordance.
#
# Do not add assignments here: no value written in this file — active or commented out — reaches
# the app, so a value that "looks configured" would silently do nothing.
